Solvent Weld PVC Pressure pipe fitting. 15 bar WP, WRAS approved (suitable for potable water) Currently in stock at our UK warehouse. Dimension Data Specifications Temperature Derating Compatibility Applications Delivery Returns Dimension Data A B C D 60.4mm 50.1mm 42.2mm 29mm Total Weight: 49g Product data subject to change without notice Specifications Material: PVC Manufacturing standards: WRAS, BS-EN1452-3, BS4346-1, 
        ISO9001, ISO14001 Jointing process: Solvent cement socket ends. For more 
        information, refer to solvent welding article. Maximum working pressure: 15bar Manufacturer: ERA* Operating temperature: 0-60°C Full specification sheet: *(We usually have plenty of these in stock; however, if we have a sudden
                large demand and run short, an alternative manufacturer's part, with the same specifications and as
                close to the same dimensions stated above, may be supplied in its place) Temperature Derating The pressure rating of PVC pipe and fittings reduces with increasing temperature. To calculate the actual 
        pressure rating of the product at each temperature, the noted pressure rating must be multiplied by the 
        'de-rating multiple', as explained on our PVC category page. The temperature derating table of this fitting is as follows: Temperature (°C) Pressure Rating (bar) 20 15 30 12 40 8.7 50 5.9 60 3.3 PVC pipe has a recommended operating temperature of 0 - 60° centigrade (32 - 140°F). Compatibility This 1 1/4" plain socket is compatible with 1 1/4" PVC pressure pipe and spigot fittings. It is not 
        compatible with metric PVC pressure pipes or fittings. 1 1/4" pipe actually has an outside diameter of 42.2mm. 1 1/4" pipes or spigot fittings (measuring 42.2mm outer diameter) will slot inside the ends of this 
        socket to be solvent welded. Applications PVC (or PVCU) is one of the most widely used plastics in general industry. Its ease of installation,
        rigidity, WRAS approval, and low price point compared to many other plastics makes it ideal for 
        applications such as: Factories and general process industries Swimming pools and spas Aquaculture, hydroponics, and aquaponics Agriculture and irrigation Water processing and treatment In addition, PVC pipe also finds its way into many domestic applications, including: Salt and freshwater aquaria Ponds and water features Home pools, hot tubs, and spas Micro irrigation Delivery The current stock status of this item is: IN STOCK for immediate dispatch by carrier. Delivery options for this item are: Next Working Day 2-3 Working Day For more information, including our order cut-off times and postcode availability, please see our delivery info page . Returns This 1 1/4" PVC plain socket is eligible for return - please see our returns page for more information. function openInfo(evt, infoName) {
        var i, tabcontent, tablinks;
        tabcontent = document.getElementsByClassName("descTabContent");
        for (i = 0; i < tabcontent.length; i++) {
            tabcontent[i].style.display = "none";
        }
        tablinks = document.getElementsByClassName("desctablinks");
        for (i = 0; i < tablinks.length; i++) {
            tablinks[i].className = tablinks[i].className.replace(" active", "");
        }
        document.getElementById(infoName).style.display = "block";
        evt.currentTarget.className += " active";
    } // Get the element with id="defaultOpen" and click on it
    document.getElementById("defaultOpen").click();

